From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vendomat Fork <vendomat-fork@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] vendomat: require a target-bound preflight before a fresh
 install writes disks

A machine with `vendomat.mode = "fresh-install"` must pass a target-side
preflight before the disko phase or the install phase. A machine with no
`vendomat.mode` is refused for every phase. A fresh-install machine with
no `vendomat.preflight.program` is refused before any target contact when
the phase set reaches disko or install.

New options: `machines.<name>.vendomat.preflight.program` (a derivation
whose output is one executable file) and
`machines.<name>.vendomat.preflight.ttlSeconds` (1 to 900, default 300).
The program is built as `machines.<name>.build.vendomatPreflight`. The
installCheck output gains `diskoDevices`, taken from the evaluated disko
layout. Every device must be a `/dev/disk/by-id/` path.

Before encryption keys, disko, or nixos-install, the CLI copies the
program to the target and runs it with a fresh 128-bit nonce:

  <program> --machine NAME --nonce HEX --phases CSV --disko-mode MODE
            --disk BYID [--disk BYID ...]

The program prints one JSON report on stdout with schema
`vendomat.preflight/v1` and exits 0 on a definite pass. The CLI accepts
the report only when it is complete, says "pass" with every check
"pass", repeats the nonce and machine name, repeats the machine-id and
boot-id that the CLI reads itself over SSH, and lists exactly the disks of
the disko layout. The result expires `ttlSeconds` after acceptance; each
disk-writing phase checks it again. Nothing in the process environment
counts as attestation.

Upstream: fork-only. Drop if upstream adds an equivalent install gate.
